---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${SITE.name}: ${SITE.tagline}`}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[44rem] px-5 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">{SITE.tagline}</h1>
    <div class="prose-nsr mt-8">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is an independent newsletter on the business of endurance sports: the companies, deals and economics behind running, triathlon, cycling and swimming.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every issue takes one company or one question (a watchmaker turned training platform, a shoe brand growing faster than the category, a race series owned by private equity) and works through what actually drives it. Where the money comes from, what it costs to make, who it competes with, and which handful of numbers you need to watch.
      </p>
      <p>
        The research leans on primary sources: annual reports, quarterly results, investor presentations and earnings calls. Numbers are sourced. Bull and bear cases get equal time.
      </p>
      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <p>Written by a finance graduate and triathlete based in Dubai.</p>
      <h2>Why "negative split"?</h2>
      <p>
        A negative split is running the second half of a race faster than the first. It takes patience, discipline and an honest read of your own numbers. Good businesses look a lot like that.
      </p>
      <p>Nothing here is investment advice. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12"><Signup compact /></div>
  </section>
</Base>
